WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.301
What to carry forward.

2
00:00:01.581 --> 00:00:05.293
The embedding model is a sticky decision, so make it with evidence.

3
00:00:05.573 --> 00:00:20.485
Use the leaderboard’s retrieval scores and your constraints (languages, input length, data location, latency, cost) to shortlist two or three candidates, including at least one provider model and one open model where policy allows.

4
00:00:20.765 --> 00:00:23.155
Set query and document roles correctly.

5
00:00:23.435 --> 00:00:32.395
Evaluate on 30 to 100 labeled queries from your domain with recall@k and MRR, compare query by query, and keep the set.

6
00:00:32.675 --> 00:00:36.813
If a Matryoshka size option exists, measure the smaller sizes too.

7
00:00:37.093 --> 00:00:45.029
Next lesson: once you have millions of vectors, how do you search them in milliseconds, and how do you know the fast search isn’t missing things?
